course: dictionary
lesson: 673
title: Baldness: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Baldness is a noun, and its adjective is bald. In its first meaning it means having little or no hair on the head. Picture a bald head: the hair has gone. «People are sensitive about how they look: wrinkles, baldness, being short or not pretty, or getting forgetful with age.» The list shows things that many people feel worried about, so sensitive means easily upset about them.
explain: Baldness can also mean the state of a surface being bare, with its usual covering gone. A worn tyre has lost the pattern that grips the road, so it looks bare. That is the baldness of a worn tyre. Always check the subject of the sentence: a head or a tyre tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: In science and health, baldness is another word for hair loss. It is often seen in older men and can sometimes be caused by illness or medicine. Phrases such as male-pattern baldness and going bald use the word in this way. Talk about it kindly, because it is a normal change that happens to many people.
fact: Baldness is a noun, and bald is the adjective: «He is bald.»
fact: «Baldness» means having little or no hair on the head.
fact: «Baldness» can also mean a surface that is bare, without its usual covering, such as a worn tyre.
fact: In science and health, baldness means hair loss, often in older men, and sometimes caused by illness or medicine.
fact: Being sensitive about looks is common, and kind words help more than teasing.
exercise: «People are sensitive about how they look: wrinkles, baldness, being short or not pretty, or getting forgetful with age.» What does baldness mean here? | Having very long, thick hair | *Having little or no hair on the head | Wearing a hat all day | Feeling tired after a long walk
exercise: A worn tyre has lost its pattern and looks bare. What does the baldness of a worn tyre mean? | Its colour fading in the sun | *The state of its surface being bare, without its usual covering | Its noise when it drives fast | Its size being too big for the car
exercise: Which word is the adjective that goes with baldness? | hair | *bald | baldness | wigs
test: In a science text, what does baldness usually describe? | A sudden change in the weather | The colour of someone's eyes | *Hair loss, often in older men | A healthy new hairstyle
test: Which sentence uses bald correctly? | The bald sky was full of stars. | The bald tyre had deep grooves for wet roads. | *The bald man laughed as he told a joke.
exam: Why are people sensitive about baldness, according to «People are sensitive about how they look: wrinkles, baldness, being short or not pretty, or getting forgetful with age»? | Because it means they cannot remember things | Because they enjoy being bald | *Because it is one of the things people may feel worried about when they think about how they look | Because it is a kind of weather
